From da73a65167cb953879a217cfbce8ffaf8c961f58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gregory R. Lee" <grelee@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 16:32:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Defer backpressure wait setup until queue pressure

Avoid constructing the timed AdaptiveWait and reading the clock on the
uncontended blocking-send path. Check receiver connectivity, channel
state, and queue fullness first, and enter the existing bounded retry
loop only when a live receiver actually exerts backpressure.

Preserve retry actions and error classification while leaving the
uncontended and disconnected paths unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending [upstream submission not yet prepared]

diff --git a/iceoryx2-cal/src/zero_copy_connection/common.rs b/iceoryx2-cal/src/zero_copy_connection/common.rs
index 7106326c..2ef89218 100644
